+     a league with offset 6 re-fetched every single DAY and only offset 0 ever got 7 days. The
+     stagger must shift WHICH day a league runs, never how often. Now a calendar slot
+     (`(ordinal + offset) % interval == 0`) with a safety net at `age >= interval`.
+
+  SCOPE AMENDMENT: `ingestion/api_football/orchestrator.py`, authority = the CPO-approved plan,
+  which specifies the read is "called ONCE per table per run and passed down, mirroring
+  `captured_player_team_seasons` (`orchestrator.py:201`)". The hoist can only live where the
+  per-competition loop is, so the approved design already required this file; its omission from
+  `scope_paths` was clerical. The contract gate caught it on the first edit.
+
+  ALSO CORRECTED, from a reviewer finding: four places in this task asserted that
+  `RAW_APIF_COACHES` is merge-on-write since 8b. It is APPEND-ONLY and was explicitly EXCLUDED
+  from 8b by the ruling of 2026-06-23 recorded above, because `stg_apif__coaches` reads ALL
+  snapshots to preserve every coach ever seen. The builder wrote that exclusion two days ago and
+  then contradicted it. The skip design is unaffected — skipping writes nothing either way —
+  but the stated reason was wrong for one of the two tables the task is about.
